{% comment %}
  Snippet: WW Product Ingredients List
  Renders the ingredients list dynamically from a Product Metafield referencing a list of Ingredient Metaobjects.

  ========================================================================================
  SHOPIFY ADMIN CUSTOM DATA CONFIGURATION GUIDE:
  ========================================================================================
  1. CREATE THE METAOBJECT (The repeater item structure):
     - Go to: Settings > Custom data > Metaobjects > Add definition.
     - Name: "Ingredient" (Shopify will automatically assign key: "ingredient").
     - Add these 3 Fields:
       * Field 1: Single line text -> Name: "Heading" (Key: "heading")
       * Field 2: Single line text -> Name: "Subheading" (Key: "subheading")
       * Field 3: Multi-line text -> Name: "Description" (Key: "description")

  2. CREATE THE PRODUCT METAFIELD (The list of ingredients):
     - Go to: Settings > Custom data > Products > Add definition.
     - Name: "Ingredients"
     - Namespace and key: "custom.ingredients"
     - Type: Select "Metaobject", and select "List of entries" (repeater).
     - Reference: Select your "Ingredient" metaobject definition.

  3. ADD DATA TO PRODUCTS:
     - Go to any Product page in your Admin, scroll to the bottom Metafields section,
       and add/link entries in your "Ingredients" list!
  ========================================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign ingredients_list = product.metafields.custom.ingredients.value -%}
{%- if ingredients_list != blank -%}
  {%- for item in ingredients_list -%}
    {%- assign heading = item.heading.value | default: item.heading -%}
    {%- assign subheading = item.subheading.value | default: item.subheading -%}
    {%- assign description = item.description.value | default: item.description -%}

    <div class="ww-ing">
      <div class="ww-ing-dot"></div>
      <div>
        <h4>
          {{ heading | escape }}
          {%- if subheading != blank -%}
            <span class="amt">{{ subheading | escape }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </h4>
        {%- if description != blank -%}
          <p>{{ description | newline_to_br }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
